@startuml SC_SimulationRun
title What-if Scenario and SimulationRun Lifecycle

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F0F6FB
  BorderColor #42566B
  FontColor #172B4D
  StartColor #253E55
  EndColor #253E55
}

[*] --> Draft : Create scenario configuration
Draft --> Draft : Edit conditions / invalid validation
Draft --> ReadyToRun : Configuration validates and saves
ReadyToRun --> Draft : Edit configuration
ReadyToRun --> Queued : Operator requests a run
Queued --> Snapshotting : Worker accepts run
Queued --> Failed : Worker unavailable
Snapshotting --> Running : Consistent baseline stored
Snapshotting --> Failed : Snapshot unavailable / inconsistent
Running --> Evaluating : Simulation horizon completed
Running --> Failed : Timeout / engine error
Evaluating --> Recommending : Impact measures calculated
Evaluating --> Failed : Evaluation error
Recommending --> Completed : Results and recommendations saved
Recommending --> Failed : Recommendation or persistence error
Completed --> Archived : Retention / Operator archive
Failed --> Archived : Retention / Operator archive
Archived --> [*]

Completed : Immutable baseline, assumptions,
Completed : results and recommendation outcome
Failed : Failure stage and diagnostics retained

note right of Running
All state changes occur in an isolated simulation copy.
The live network is never updated by this lifecycle.
end note

note right of Failed
A retry creates a new run record so the failed run
remains auditable and is never rewritten as Completed.
end note
@enduml
